          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.15,
          "end": 39.63,
          "en": "that this code never ends up on the front end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.63,
          "end": 42.96,
          "en": "Because of course, especially for the auth related code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.96,
          "end": 46.59,
          "en": "you wanna ensure that this code does not accidentally end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.59,
          "end": 48.36,
          "en": "up in your front end code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.36,
          "end": 51.873,
          "en": "because it could contain security relevant details.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.01,
          "end": 58.01,
          "en": "So here I'll export an async function called \"signup.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.08,
          "end": 59.04,
          "en": "Like this:",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.04,
          "end": 59.873,
          "en": "And async",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.873,
          "end": 62.52,
          "en": "because we'll use some async operations in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.52,
          "end": 66.27,
          "en": "And in this function we now wanna create a new user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.27,
          "end": 69.66,
          "en": "For that, here I expect to get some credentials.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.66,
          "end": 72.27,
          "en": "An object with a email and password field.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.27,
          "end": 76.56,
          "en": "And therefore we can also use object destructuring here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.56,
          "end": 81.21000000000001,
          "en": "And then here we get a couple of things that should be done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.21000000000001,
          "end": 82.83,
          "en": "For example, we wanna check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 82.83,
          "end": 86.19,
          "en": "whether a user with that email exists already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.19,
          "end": 91.02,
          "en": "Sure, I added this unique constraint in my schema",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.02,
          "end": 94.83,
          "en": "and therefore MongoDB should actually prevent us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 94.83,
          "end": 98.82,
          "en": "from adding an extra user with an existing email.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.82,
          "end": 101.22,
          "en": "But still I wanna add my own check here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.22,
          "end": 104.40299999999999,
          "en": "And for that, we can simply use Prisma.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.36,
          "end": 108.09,
          "en": "Importing it from the \"database.server\" file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 108.09,
          "end": 110.94,
          "en": "where we set up this Prisma connection.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 110.94,
          "end": 112.08,
          "en": "And on Prisma",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 112.08,
          "end": 115.41,
          "en": "we now got a user field thanks to our updated schema",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 115.41,
          "end": 119.4,
          "en": "and thanks to us running: \"npx prisma db push.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 119.4,
          "end": 123.87,
          "en": "And here I first of all wanna check if we have a user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 123.87,
          "end": 127.53,
          "en": "I simply wanna find the first user where",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 127.53,
          "end": 130.05,
          "en": "the email field is equal to our email,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 130.05,
          "end": 131.16,
          "en": "and we can use the shortcut",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 131.16,
          "end": 133.65,
          "en": "here of just writing email since we have the same names",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 133.65,
          "end": 137.64,
          "en": "for the property name and the variable that contains",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 137.64,
          "end": 138.93,
          "en": "the value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 138.93,
          "end": 142.65,
          "en": "So here I wanna get an existing user with that email.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 142.65,
          "end": 145.89,
          "en": "Now if we do get such a existing user, that's a problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 145.89,
          "end": 148.65,
          "en": "That means we already have a user with that email",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 148.65,
          "end": 151.293,
          "en": "and that means we can't create a new user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 152.34,
          "end": 156.12,
          "en": "In this case, I'll create a new error object here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 156.12,
          "end": 157.417,
          "en": "Where I'll just say:",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 157.417,
          "end": 162.417,
          "en": "\"A user with the provided email address exists already\",",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 163.59,
          "end": 165.57,
          "en": "and I'll add an extra property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 165.57,
          "end": 167.25,
          "en": "to this error object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 167.25,
          "end": 169.86,
          "en": "a status property of 422.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 169.86,
          "end": 172.74,
          "en": "422 is a common HTTP status code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 172.74,
          "end": 175.59,
          "en": "for indicating incorrect user input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 175.59,
          "end": 178.11,
          "en": "But this is not an error response here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 178.11,
          "end": 179.85,
          "en": "I'm just using this code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 179.85,
          "end": 182.61,
          "en": "in accordance with HTTP status codes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 182.61,
          "end": 184.86,
          "en": "But this is not an error response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 184.86,
          "end": 188.16,
          "en": "This is a regular JavaScript error object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 188.16,
          "end": 192.393,
          "en": "and I'm throwing it as a regular JavaScript object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 193.62,
          "end": 194.55,
          "en": "So right now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 194.55,
          "end": 197.61,
          "en": "this would trigger our error boundary components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 197.61,
          "end": 199.8,
          "en": "not the catch boundary components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 199.8,
          "end": 202.2,
          "en": "because this is not an error response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 202.2,
          "end": 204.96,
          "en": "but I'll handle it differently anyways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 204.96,
          "end": 207.78,
          "en": "But before I handle it differently, let's continue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 207.78,
          "end": 210.933,
          "en": "with the rest of the code of this signup logic.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
